{"success": true, "message": "Test details sent successfully", "data": {"test": {"_id": "69de21f57e39d99b57bc5b55", "analysisVideoCdn": "yt", "exam": ["605dfcb2f226ac25a8bd5fef"], "ctype": null, "position": 0, "order": 12, "enableCalculator": false, "isContinuousQuestion": false, "reattemptAvailable": false, "singleSectionMultipleSubjects": false, "timeRestricted": false, "title": "Ionic Equilibrium - Test 3", "description": "Previous Year Questions as Chapter Test", "syllabus": "This test contains questions from all topics of this chapter included in the JEE Main syllabus. It includes a mix of questions from PYQs of JEE Main 2019 - 2025.", "totalTime": 30, "totalQuestions": 20, "totalMarks": 80, "bonusQuestions": null, "bonusMarks": null, "startDate": "2026-04-15T03:30:00.000Z", "endDate": "2027-04-30T00:00:00.000Z", "type": "free", "class": "605df635a37b7025c438d685", "instruction": "608289ffb160b022e9442c83", "subjects": [{"subjectId": "607018ee404ae53194e73d91", "totalMarks": 80, "bonusMarks": 0, "totalQuestions": 20, "bonusQuestions": 0, "_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc674"}], "sections": [{"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc671", "title": "Chemistry Numerical", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d91", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc60a", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df89"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b72"], "concepts": ["6162fb966ed13040ec850a63"], "question": {"text": "The <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>pH</mi></math> of a solution obtained by mixing <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mL</mi></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>HCl</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mL</mi></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>NaOH</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math> is (Nearest integer)<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3979</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>"}, "options": [{"id": "d8915a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc60b"}, {"id": "b21615", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc60c"}, {"id": "e4e336", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc60d"}, {"id": "536981", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc60e"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc60f", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df89"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b478f"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b46"], "question": {"text": "At <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>310</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>, the solubility of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CaF</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> in water is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>34</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mL</mi></math>. The solubility product of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CaF</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> is ----&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>mol</mi><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>3</mn></msup></math>(nearest integer). (Given molar mass : <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CaF</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>78</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>)"}, "options": [{"id": "25765c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc610"}, {"id": "82b3d5", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc611"}, {"id": "361f88", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc612"}, {"id": "6153eb", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc613"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc614", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df89"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4776"], "concepts": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52d4"], "question": {"text": "<p>A litre of buffer solution contains <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;mole of each of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mi>Cl</mi></math>. On the addition of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>02</mn></math>&nbsp;mole of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>HCl</mi></math> by dissolving gaseous <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>HCl</mi></math>, the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>pH</mi></math> of the solution is found to be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;(Nearest integer)</p><p>Given:&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>pK</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></msub><mfenced><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>745</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>log</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>301</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>log</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>477</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>298</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>]</mo></math></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "91d59a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc615"}, {"id": "649dfe", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc616"}, {"id": "15feb6", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc617"}, {"id": "446f9e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc618"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc619", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df89"], "topics": ["60e5676a499d1e49588f8f0d"], "concepts": ["6162fb956ed13040ec850977"], "question": {"text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>01</mn></math> moles of a weak acid <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>HA</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math> is dissolved in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>HCl</mi></math> solution. The degree of dissociation of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>HA</mi></math> is&nbsp;__________&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></math> (Round off to the Nearest Integer). [Neglect volume change on adding <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>HA</mi></math>&nbsp;and assume degree of dissociation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#60;</mo><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>1</mn></math>]</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "1ed51d", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc61a"}, {"id": "e66afa", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc61b"}, {"id": "8e0e24", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc61c"}, {"id": "966f70", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc61d"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc61e", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df89"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f4c"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f13"], "question": {"text": "<p>On complete reaction of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>FeCl</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> with oxalic acid in aqueous solution containing <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>KOH</mi></math>, resulted in the formation of product <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>. The secondary valency of Fe in the product A&nbsp;is ______ .</p><p>(Round off to the Nearest Integer).</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "4c939f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc61f"}, {"id": "b8fcac", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc620"}, {"id": "2d6c70", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc621"}, {"id": "f4f082", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc622"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc623", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df89"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b72"], "concepts": ["6162fb966ed13040ec850a5d"], "question": {"text": "If 1 mM solution of ethylamine produces $\\mathrm{pH}=9$, then the ionization constant $\\left(\\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{b}}\\right)$ of ethylamine is $10^{-x}$. The value of $x$ is ______ (nearest integer).\n[The degree of ionization of ethylamine can be neglected with respect to unity.]"}, "options": [{"id": "dee7a1", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc624"}, {"id": "dc83b1", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc625"}, {"id": "749255", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc626"}, {"id": "6df02f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc627"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc628", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df89"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b478f"], "concepts": ["6162fb986ed13040ec850c20"], "question": {"text": "The <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>pH</mi></math> at which <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Mg</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>OH</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mo> </mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi>sp</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math> begins to precipitate from a solution containing <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>10</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Mg</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> ions is ______."}, "options": [{"id": "1605d4", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc629"}, {"id": "564c90", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc62a"}, {"id": "9a2c22", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc62b"}, {"id": "78cba8", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc62c"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc62d", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df89"], "topics": ["60e5676a499d1e49588f8f0d"], "concepts": ["6162fb956ed13040ec850979"], "question": {"text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>ml</mi></math>&nbsp;of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Na</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> solution is titrated against <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>HCl</mi></math>&nbsp;solution. The following&nbsp;values were obtained in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math> readings.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>ml</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>ml</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>ml</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>ml</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>ml</mi></math>&nbsp;</p><p>Based on these readings, and convention of titrimetric estimation of concentration of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Na</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> solution is ___&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>mM</mi></math>.<br />(Round off to the Nearest integer)</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "0ea745", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc62e"}, {"id": "a734c1", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc62f"}, {"id": "3c8cea", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc630"}, {"id": "0aab38", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc631"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc632", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df89"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4776"], "concepts": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52d4"], "question": {"text": "In order to prepare a buffer solution of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>pH</mi><mn>5</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>74</mn></math>, sodium acetate is added to acetic acid. If the concentration of acetic acid in the buffer is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;the concentration of sodium acetate in the buffer is ______<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>.</mo></math> (Round off to the Nearest Integer).&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Given</mi><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>pKa</mi><mfenced><mtext>acetic&#160;acid</mtext></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>74</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>"}, "options": [{"id": "bfe01d", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc633"}, {"id": "d0d4f5", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc634"}, {"id": "c99064", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc635"}, {"id": "2db8fd", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc636"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc637", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df89"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b72"], "concepts": ["60e567fb499d1e49588fa029"], "question": {"text": "<p>An analyst wants to convert <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>HCl</mi></math>&nbsp;of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>pH</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> to a solution of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>HCl</mi></math>&nbsp;of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>pH</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>. The volume of water needed to do this dilution is _____ <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>mL</mi></math>. (Nearest integer)</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "62cc8a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc638"}, {"id": "06419e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc639"}, {"id": "384c0a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc63a"}, {"id": "ae131e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc63b"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc63c", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df89"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b478f"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b4748"], "question": {"text": "The solubility product of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>BaSO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></msup></math> at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>298</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>. The solubility of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>BaSO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mi>aq</mi><mo>)</mo></math> solution is&nbsp; &nbsp; ------<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>(nearest integer).<br />Given: Molar mass of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>BaSO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>233</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>"}, "options": [{"id": "ac86ac", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc63d"}, {"id": "6df8ff", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc63e"}, {"id": "adb13c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc63f"}, {"id": "1f96db", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc640"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc641", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df89"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b72"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f32"], "question": {"text": "Millimoles of calcium hydroxyide required to produce <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mi>mL</mi></math> of the aqueous solution of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>pH</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>12</mn></math>&nbsp;is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is _____ (Nearest integer).<br />Assume complete dissociation."}, "options": [{"id": "fca3ad", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc642"}, {"id": "c89659", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc643"}, {"id": "0a6cff", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc644"}, {"id": "ad130e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc645"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc646", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df89"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b478f"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e55"], "question": {"text": "<p>The molar solubility of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">