leapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F12ef0859-3b37-4d9c-9427-f3c6df4364b6.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 246px;\" /></p><p>The number of following statement/s which is/are correct about phenolphthalein is _______</p><p>A. It can be used as an indicator for the titration of weak acid with weak base.</p><p>B. It begins to change colour at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>pH</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p><p>C. It is a weak organic base</p><p>D. It is colourless in acidic medium</p><p>&nbsp;</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "9e13eb", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc64c"}, {"id": "336a40", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc64d"}, {"id": "b3504e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc64e"}, {"id": "38321e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc64f"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc650", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df89"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b478f"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b46"], "question": {"text": "At <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>298</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>, the solubility of silver chloride in water is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>434</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>logK</mi><mi>sp</mi></msub></math> for silver chloride is<br />(Given mass of Ag is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>107</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>, and mass of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Cl</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>35</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> )"}, "options": [{"id": "71d5c9", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc651"}, {"id": "4d63e3", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc652"}, {"id": "dd7064", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc653"}, {"id": "d70e59", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc654"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc655", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df89"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b72"], "concepts": ["6162fb966ed13040ec850a5a"], "question": {"text": "The <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>pH</mi></math> of ammonium phosphate solution, if <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>pk</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></msub></math> of phosphoric acid and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>pk</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></msub></math> of ammonium hydroxide are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>23</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>75</mn></math> respectively, is"}, "options": [{"id": "ef90e3", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc656"}, {"id": "4d457b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc657"}, {"id": "246e34", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc658"}, {"id": "a3c5ef", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc659"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f01c677dc36a88fc65a", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e84